IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part3`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part3.l4 (ss 25(1), (2), (4), (5), 26).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part III, the parts that are not time computations`

-- s 25(1) and (2).  Arguments: commences on the passing; provision itself confers the power; provision would amend
-- another Act so that it confers the power; the power is of a listed kind; the Act has been passed; necessary or expedient.
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the power may be exercised before the provision commences` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- s 25(4)
#ASSERT `the appointee may act in the office, or the body may meet and perform its functions` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointee may act in the office, or the body may meet and perform its functions` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the earliest day the term of office of an early appointee begins` (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS Date 1 7 2025

-- s 25(5) with s 3(3)
#ASSERT `section 25 applies to the Act` (Date 1 1 1985) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 25 applies to the Act` (Date 1 7 1984) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 25 applies to the Act` (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 25 applies to the Act` (Date 1 1 1990) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 26(1), (2): sufficient citations
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the short title or the citation given to it or by which it was made citable` `an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the short title or the citation given to it or by which it was made citable` `subsidiary legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year` `an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the year-and-number form is given for Acts only: for subsidiary legislation the Act says nothing
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the year in which it was passed and its number among the Acts of that year` `subsidiary legislation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division in which a provision is contained` `an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `the Part, section, regulation, rule, clause or other division in which a provision is contained` `subsidiary legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a citation is sufficient for all purposes` `some other form of citation` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(3)
#ASSERT `a citation or reference is made as the Act requires` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a citation or reference is made as the Act requires` FALSE)
